  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1013 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nThe theme for next week will be daily chances of convective chances \nbeneath a mid-level moisture plume favoring areas on the caprock. \nThe upper level ridge will further move eastward to the southeastern \nCONUS. This will allow the monsoon moisture plume to shift more \noverhead starting as early as Monday but increasing in coverage \naloft for the rest of the week. With the ridge moving farther away \nfrom the region and an increase in moisture will result in a \nlowering trend on temperatures through the week. The cooler surface \ntemperatures will bring minimal chances of severe convection with \nsmaller inverted-V soundings and lower cloud bases. Tuesday and \nafternoon and evening may see increased precipitation chances with a \ncold front making a run at the region but likely stopping shy of the \narea in the Texas Panhandle. A second cold front will make a run at \nthe area on Thursday with better chances of reaching into the South \nPlains. It is this second cold front which may finally bring \ntemperatures back down towards seasonal averages next weekend with \nmodels showing easterly upslope flow during this time period.",
